<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2015/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>pisum-whisper</id>
    <!-- Rewritten from the tag by release.yml before `choco pack`, so this value is the
         development default and never what is published. -->
    <version>0.1.0</version>
    <title>Pisum Whisper</title>
    <authors>Michael Schnecke</authors>
    <owners>mschnecke</owners>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/mschnecke/pisum-whisper</projectUrl>
    <licenseUrl>https://github.com/mschnecke/pisum-whisper/blob/main/LICENSE</licenseUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <description>
Pisum Whisper is a hotkey-driven dictation utility. Hold a global hotkey to record speech, release to transcribe it with Google Gemini, and the transcript is pasted at the cursor position in whatever application you were already typing in.

- Hold-to-record or toggle, on a hotkey you choose and can rebind without a restart
- Transcription through Google Gemini, with a round-robin pool of API keys and categorised failures
- Per-preset system prompts, so the same speech can be formatted differently
- Tray-resident: no taskbar button and no window until you ask for one, with the icon reporting idle, recording or transcribing
- Settings saved as you type them, and a rolling log at %USERPROFILE%\.pisum-whisper\logs

Needs a Google Gemini API key, which you enter on the settings window's Providers tab.
    </description>
    <summary>Hotkey-driven dictation that pastes the transcript at the cursor</summary>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/mschnecke/pisum-whisper/releases</releaseNotes>
    <copyright>Copyright 2026 Michael Schnecke</copyright>
    <tags>dictation transcription speech-to-text gemini hotkey tray admin</tags>
    <packageSourceUrl>https://github.com/mschnecke/pisum-whisper/tree/main/packaging/chocolatey</packageSourceUrl>
    <docsUrl>https://github.com/mschnecke/pisum-whisper#readme</docsUrl>
    <bugTrackerUrl>https://github.com/mschnecke/pisum-whisper/issues</bugTrackerUrl>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
